Comment: 
// @@@ If the index is valid (non-negative and less than the initial size of the list), then for every valid index i before the specified index, either both the current and old values at i are null, or the current value at i is equal to its old value.

Interpretation: In set method, precondition: index valid (0 <= index < old size). Then after operation, for all i such that 0 <= i < index, we have either both current and old values at i are null, or current value equals old value. Equivalent: For all i in [0, index), (this.get(i) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i))). Need to handle null safe equality.

